{"version":"0.12.31","prev_tag":"v0.12.30","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"76f0879faef6926c170bf7e25067fdffdf405cb7","title":"Make bare lf a general-purpose conversation and add lf operate (#1393)","files":["README.md","docs/getting-started.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/default.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/repo_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/review-open-work.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/skills.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/default_conversation_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/terminal_control_tests.rs","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_realign.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.md"]},{"sha":"0713854d5359ab83e724d936fa3dffeafb43252e","title":"Make Doctor diagnose machine commands and keep cron working across installs (#1402)","files":["README.md","docs/architecture/environment.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/cron.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/doctor_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs"]},{"sha":"fac48dd22ba8f98dc45174549cb1e281ce340db8","title":"Fix Codex Flow decisions and release completion after CI repair (#1401)","files":["TESTING.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_output.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/release_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"f889f071bbd27ad4a7e37230e272ebe7f6da827c","title":"Make Doctor diagnose broken Homes without changing their schema (#1404)","files":["docs/troubleshooting.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/doctor_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"2064555c4418e153474505a19379189692dcaa21","title":"Advance Tasks with task/operate and open blocking Sessions in Desktop (#1405)","files":["README.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_operate.md","swift/LoopflowMac/PodiumModel.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/SessionsView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkspacePalette.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/WorkspaceDestination.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/WorkspaceDestinationTests.swift","swift/README.md"]},{"sha":"101a19b8c5008705a6a527779c6fd6666f0c2637","title":"Keep current Tasks visible and browse completed history inline (#1403)","files":["docs/reviews/task-history.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/planning_lookup_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_comments_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_planning_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_actions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/linear.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/planning.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/dto_fixtures.rs","swift/Loopflow/Models/TaskStatus.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/WaveWorkMap.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/MockWaveFixture.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/PodiumModel.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/TaskHistoryFilter.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/RoadmapView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WaveDetailPane.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkSurfaceView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/WorkspaceProjection.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/DTOFixtureTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/TaskHistoryFilterTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/WaveLensTests.swift","swift/README.md","tests/e2e/task_deletion.py","tests/fixtures/dto/pm_show.json","tests/fixtures/dto/roadmap_snapshot.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_condition_states.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_history_planning.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_history_rows.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_status.json","tests/fixtures/dto/wave_detail.json","wave/product/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"f4dfc620188aa16b78331c17e68cff2b00b32949","title":"Keep release publication compatible with the installed CLI (#1406)","files":["python/tests/test_release_publisher.py","scripts/publish_release.py","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"05d4dd1a025b77cdf2813a37cb28ba9f9cc377af","title":"release: v0.12.31 (#1407)","files":["Cargo.lock","Cargo.toml","RELEASE_NOTES.md","pyproject.toml","release/v0.12.31/NOTES.md","rust/loopflow/src/store/migration_catalog.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/0.12.31.001_release.sql","rust/loopflow/src/store/migrations/drafts/remove_ask.sql","uv.lock"]},{"sha":"a1afb5fde04690b20e728a60aea7fd1cf66dabe6","title":"Recover releases when concurrent merges leave migrations unprepared (#1408)","files":[".github/workflows/package-build.yml","docs/architecture-reference.md","performance/budgets.json","python/tests/test_checkout_refresh.py","python/tests/test_release_publisher.py","python/tests/test_resource_envelope.py","release/README.md","rust/loopflow/src/journal/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/top.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/src/session_record.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite.rs","rust/loopflow/src/work/wave/context.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/release_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/wave_resolution_matrix.rs","scripts/publish_release.py","scripts/resource_envelope.py","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/TaskRunsProofTests.swift"]},{"sha":"36446011acf7062f42b797660d17dbf3548d6777","title":"Persist Session completion before capture finish returns (#1409)","files":["rust/loopflow/src/session_record.rs"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1393,"title":"Make bare lf a general-purpose conversation and add lf operate","body":"Bare `lf` previously opened a repository control conversation that checked Sessions on every turn and directed work elsewhere. It now follows the request and can work in the current checkout, with repository operations available explicitly through `lf operate`.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add a lightweight default skill that answers questions and follows changing direction without requiring a repository inventory.\n- Consolidate the former `loopflow` and `review-open-work` skills into `repo/operate`, covering cleanup, activity summaries, Wave progression, and Task capture. The retired skill names are removed.\n- Resolve `lf operate` to `repo/operate`; keep `wave/operate` explicit and preserve repository skill overrides.\n- Keep bare `lf` in its launching terminal. Repository operation honors launch flags and configuration.\n- Update documentation and regression coverage for prompt separation, skill discovery, launch selection, and skill exports.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded branch checks passed: skill export tests, the focused discovery test, `cargo fmt`, and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`. These were not rerun for this description. The launch regression uses a simulated provider; it does not verify a live conversation.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed here: run `lf` and ask a question unrelated to repository management. The conversation should answer directly without first listing Sessions. Then run `lf operate` and request a summary of open work; it should inspect repository activity and identify useful next actions.","files":[],"additions":482,"deletions":411,"changed_files":19,"merge_commit":"76f0879faef6926c170bf7e25067fdffdf405cb7"},{"number":1401,"title":"Fix Codex Flow decisions and release completion after CI repair","body":"Codex could reject the Flow decision schema, and releases could stop on stale CI failures after repair and merge completed. Require nullable explanation fields in the provider schema while preserving historical receipts, and resume release settlement when fresh GitHub evidence confirms the merge.\n\nValidation: the new deterministic release regression failed before the repair and passed afterward. All 85 selected tests passed against the materialized migration schema: release_tests, pr_landing, Task completion, and Flow output. cargo fmt --all -- --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, and git diff --check passed. CI on the published head remains pending.","files":[],"additions":102,"deletions":15,"changed_files":6,"merge_commit":"fac48dd22ba8f98dc45174549cb1e281ce340db8"},{"number":1402,"title":"Make Doctor diagnose machine commands and keep cron working across installs","body":"Doctor treated valid machine-level Execs as corrupt history, while scheduled jobs could remain pinned to binaries retired by an installation change. This PR corrects that diagnosis, gives missing receipts actionable context, and makes newly reconciled jobs follow the stable machine entry gate.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Accept absent Exec repository scope; continue rejecting relative repository paths.\n- Include configured executable, log path, and Wave or repository reconciliation commands for missing scheduled receipts. Keep those failures visible.\n- Use the stable machine CLI gate for scheduled work and CI-watch installation; existing Sessions keep their runtime ownership.\n- Bound freshness output to three recent commits and direct installation to published releases.\n- Retain this branch's installation repair: download, promotion, rollback, and recovery no longer depend on Task PR authority; installation checks remain intact.\n\n## Checks\n\nDoctor unit tests (10), cron unit tests (16), Doctor CLI tests (3), installation regressions (2), local promotion tests (2), formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, and README/index sync passed.\n\nAn isolated replay of 3,990 unchanged production Execs reports valid identity, including 71 repository-free Execs, while preserving the two missing cron failures. The installed cron logs show startup refusal from a pinned inactive binary. Disposable gate replacement also preserves the installed job and produces a successful scheduled receipt.\n\n## Acceptance limits\n\nA full old-database copy was correctly rejected by the disposable Home's canonical-frontier contract; the history replay is not upgrade proof. Published upgrade and interrupted-switch recovery remain unverified. Live cron recovery requires installing a release containing this change, reconciling the jobs, and observing a real scheduled receipt. No release job was triggered merely to make Doctor pass.","files":[],"additions":216,"deletions":90,"changed_files":13,"merge_commit":"0713854d5359ab83e724d936fa3dffeafb43252e"},{"number":1403,"title":"Keep current Tasks visible and browse completed history inline","body":"Wave Task lists mixed current work with settled history, making unfinished Tasks harder to find. This PR shows current work by default and adds a compact control for browsing successful completions without hiding unresolved execution or losing access to retained Sessions.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Keep current Tasks visible and completed history out of the way · LOO-369](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-369/keep-current-tasks-visible-and-completed-history-out-of-the-way)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add a Completed control beside the Tasks heading and visible count. It starts with a seven-day range, supports inline editing, and remembers the range when toggled off. Entering 0 shows All Tasks, including successful completions of any age.\n- Keep settled canceled and duplicate Tasks out of completion history. Preserve visibility for unresolved execution and access to Tasks with retained Sessions.\n- Carry Linear workflow state and completion dates through storage and Rust/Swift projections. Unknown completion dates appear only in unbounded history; no dates are inferred.\n- Align Start availability and explanations with planning state so canceled, duplicate, and completed inventory cannot start new work.\n\n## Checks\n\nThe [recorded gate review](docs/reviews/task-history.md) reports 142 Rust tests and 100 selected headless Swift tests passing, plus formatting, all-target Clippy, architecture checks, Swift boundary checks, and signed Xcode build-for-testing. Coverage includes filtering, visible counts, actions, inline editing, and native glyph alignment. Checks were not rerun for this PR description.\n\nThe full test matrix remains with CI. Native visual/focus review, live Growth refresh, and real retained Session continuation remain unverified.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough: open a Wave containing current and completed Tasks. Click Completed to include the last seven days, click 7 Days and enter 30, then enter 0 for All Tasks. Rows and the heading count should follow the range while current work stays visible. Settled canceled and duplicate Tasks should remain absent. Enter an invalid range to confirm that validation preserves the previous selection; press Escape while editing to cancel.","files":[],"additions":2432,"deletions":79,"changed_files":37,"merge_commit":"101a19b8c5008705a6a527779c6fd6666f0c2637"},{"number":1404,"title":"Make Doctor diagnose broken Homes without changing their schema","body":"Doctor now inspects storage before ordinary startup admission, so missing or incompatible databases produce diagnostics without initialization or migration. Readable Exec evidence, scheduler obligations, and installation checks remain available when schema validation fails. Binary freshness uses cached origin/main and explicitly reports that limit, without fetching.\n\nValidated with six Doctor integration tests, twelve focused unit tests, cargo fmt, and cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings. Tests cover absent and corrupt databases, future migration history, machine-scoped Execs, and telemetry continuity.\n\nThe supplied LOO-367 idle observation has since changed to running kickoff. This PR does not claim to repair its original launch timeout or missing scheduled invocations.","files":[],"additions":154,"deletions":51,"changed_files":4,"merge_commit":"f889f071bbd27ad4a7e37230e272ebe7f6da827c"},{"number":1405,"title":"Advance Tasks with task/operate and open blocking Sessions in Desktop","body":"Moving a Task forward required piecing together its Flow state and finding the conversation that needed attention. The new `task/operate` skill guides that work through completion or a concrete blocker, with a command to open the exact blocking Session in Loopflow Desktop.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add `lf task/operate` instructions to read existing work, preserve unfinished Flows, resolve routine failures, and ask for judgment in the current conversation. Headless runs stop at blockers; review and delivery authority remain explicit.\n- Extend Task links with an optional `session` query that opens an existing conversation through Desktop’s normal Session-opening path, including Sessions found on later result pages.\n- Check Session membership against the runtime Task identity. Missing or unrelated Sessions preserve the current workspace and offer Retry.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded branch checks passed: 12 headless `WorkspaceDestinationTests`, builtin skill discovery, and built CLI help. No live Task was launched; the complete interactive workflow remains unverified.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed: run `lf task/operate \"<issue>\"` for a Task awaiting review. When it reports the blocking Session, run the returned `open` command. Desktop should open that existing conversation in its terminal pane without completing the review or starting another Flow.","files":[],"additions":179,"deletions":6,"changed_files":8,"merge_commit":"2064555c4418e153474505a19379189692dcaa21"},{"number":1406,"title":"Keep release publication compatible with the installed CLI","body":"The v0.12.30 publisher stopped because the installed CLI rejects lf repo release publish. Use lf release publish for staging and finalization so the verified candidate can finish through the existing release operation. Also retain infrastructure acceptance evidence and the disposition of inactive development stores in Wave memory. Validation: six focused publisher tests passed; diff check passed.","files":[],"additions":58,"deletions":3,"changed_files":3,"merge_commit":"f4dfc620188aa16b78331c17e68cff2b00b32949"},{"number":1407,"title":"release: v0.12.31","body":"# v0.12.31\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.31 makes it easier to start a conversation, find unfinished work and reach the Session that needs attention. Bare `lf` follows your request in the current checkout, while explicit operators handle repository and Task progression. Doctor can inspect broken Homes without changing their schema, and delivery fixes address stale CI failures and release-publisher compatibility.\n\n## Start with the request, reach for operations when needed\n\nOrdinary conversations no longer begin with a repository inventory or direct all work elsewhere. Repository and Task operations have explicit entry points that preserve existing work and review boundaries.\n\n- Bare `lf` opens a general-purpose conversation in the launching terminal and can work in the current checkout.\n- `lf operate` resolves to `repo/operate` for repository cleanup, activity summaries, Wave progression and Task capture. Repository skill overrides remain supported; `wave/operate` stays explicit.\n- `lf task/operate \"<issue>\"` guides a Task through existing work, routine failures and unfinished Flows until completion or a concrete blocker. Headless runs stop when required judgment is missing; review and delivery authority remain explicit.\n- Task links can name an existing Session with a `session` query, opening the blocking conversation in Desktop. Missing or unrelated Sessions leave the current workspace intact and offer Retry.\n\n## Keep current Tasks in view\n\nWave Task lists now emphasize current work, with successful completions available inline. Unresolved execution remains visible, and retained Sessions remain accessible.\n\n- The **Completed** control starts with the last seven days. Edit the range inline, or enter **0** for All Tasks; toggling it off remembers the selected range.\n- Settled canceled and duplicate Tasks stay out of completion history. Unknown completion dates appear only in unbounded history, without inferred dates.\n- Start availability and explanations follow planning state, preventing canceled, duplicate and completed inventory from starting new work.\n\n## Diagnose failures without changing the evidence\n\nDoctor runs storage inspection before ordinary startup admission. Missing or incompatible databases can therefore produce diagnostics without initialization or migration, while readable execution evidence, scheduler obligations and installation checks remain available.\n\n- Valid machine-level Execs no longer appear corrupt merely because they have no repository scope. Relative repository paths still fail validation.\n- Missing scheduled receipts remain visible, with the configured executable, log path and reconciliation commands needed to investigate.\n- Binary freshness reports use cached `origin/main`, explicitly identify that limit and show at most three recent commits without fetching.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Scheduled work:** newly reconciled jobs and CI-watch installations use the stable machine CLI entry point, avoiding binaries retired by installation changes. Existing Sessions retain their runtime ownership. Recovering affected live cron jobs requires installing this release, reconciling the jobs and observing a real scheduled receipt.\n- **Installation:** download, promotion, rollback and recovery no longer depend on Task PR authority. Installation checks remain in place, and installation guidance points to published releases.\n- **Release settlement:** fresh GitHub evidence of a completed merge now lets settlement resume after CI repair instead of stopping on stale failures. The publisher uses `lf release publish` for staging and finalization, fixing the installed-CLI incompatibility that stopped the v0.12.30 publisher.\n- **Skill names:** the former `loopflow` and `review-open-work` skills are consolidated into `repo/operate`; the retired names are removed.\n- **Acceptance limits:** supplied evidence includes focused Rust, Swift and publisher tests. Published upgrade and interrupted-switch recovery, live cron recovery, the complete interactive Task operator workflow, and native Tas","files":[],"additions":82,"deletions":49,"changed_files":8,"merge_commit":"05d4dd1a025b77cdf2813a37cb28ba9f9cc377af"},{"number":1408,"title":"Recover releases when concurrent merges leave migrations unprepared","body":"A migration merged during release preparation could leave an uninstallable candidate stuck in retries. This PR detects that source state, prepares a successor patch when publication is confirmed absent, and requires packaged candidates to pass installer preflight.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Inspect the exact merged commit before building or tagging. Preserve existing tags and canonical migrations; stop for reconciliation when publication is partial or unknown.\n- Let interrupted minor releases adopt a corrected closing patch from the same version cycle, including one published before its receipt was saved.\n- Validate packaged CLIs in a fresh disposable Home during package smoke checks, cached preparation reuse, and publication.\n- Rename repository journal evidence to Execs and traces, using `.lf/journal/traces`, `trace_id`, and `node: exec`. Session captures retain their existing `~/.lf/runs` layout and remain excluded from automatic cleanup.\n\nConfigured publishers must now support the documented `inspect` command. Consumers of repository journal files must use the new path and field names.\n\n## Checks\n\nThe recorded branch gate passed architecture checks, Python (316), Rust (2,097; 16 skipped), website (78; 3 skipped), headless Swift, and static checks. Regression coverage includes candidate replacement, partial publication, exact-commit inspection, cached artifact rejection, and interrupted minor recovery.\n\nRelease recovery was exercised with simulated providers. Live concurrent-merge recovery, publication, and installation remain unverified; hosted package preflight remains CI-owned. Checks were not rerun for this description.","files":[],"additions":925,"deletions":466,"changed_files":21,"merge_commit":"a1afb5fde04690b20e728a60aea7fd1cf66dabe6"},{"number":1409,"title":"Persist Session completion before capture finish returns","body":"The v0.12.31 merge-queue test observed a completed capture without its terminal outcome. Completion was sent through the best-effort telemetry queue, whose drain waits only 250 ms. Persist terminal outcomes synchronously through the existing Session history owner; keep stream telemetry asynchronous and retain prepared captures that have no admitted Session. Repeated settlement preserves the original terminal receipt. A deterministic regression disables the recorder and removes capture artifacts before reading the outcome from SQLite. Validation: 28 Session-record tests, the failing telemetry scorecard test, cargo fmt, and all-target Clippy passed. This repair is separate from the already selected v0.12.31 release snapshot.","files":[],"additions":50,"deletions":9,"changed_files":1,"merge_commit":"36446011acf7062f42b797660d17dbf3548d6777"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.31\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.31 makes it easier to start a conversation, find unfinished work and reach the Session that needs attention. Bare `lf` follows your request in the current checkout, while explicit operators handle repository and Task progression. Doctor can inspect broken Homes without changing their schema, and delivery fixes address stale CI failures and release-publisher compatibility.\n\n## Start with the request, reach for operations when needed\n\nOrdinary conversations no longer begin with a repository inventory or direct all work elsewhere. Repository and Task operations have explicit entry points that preserve existing work and review boundaries.\n\n- Bare `lf` opens a general-purpose conversation in the launching terminal and can work in the current checkout.\n- `lf operate` resolves to `repo/operate` for repository cleanup, activity summaries, Wave progression and Task capture. Repository skill overrides remain supported; `wave/operate` stays explicit.\n- `lf task/operate \"<issue>\"` guides a Task through existing work, routine failures and unfinished Flows until completion or a concrete blocker. Headless runs stop when required judgment is missing; review and delivery authority remain explicit.\n- Task links can name an existing Session with a `session` query, opening the blocking conversation in Desktop. Missing or unrelated Sessions leave the current workspace intact and offer Retry.\n\n## Keep current Tasks in view\n\nWave Task lists now emphasize current work, with successful completions available inline. Unresolved execution remains visible, and retained Sessions remain accessible.\n\n- The **Completed** control starts with the last seven days. Edit the range inline, or enter **0** for All Tasks; toggling it off remembers the selected range.\n- Settled canceled and duplicate Tasks stay out of completion history. Unknown completion dates appear only in unbounded history, without inferred dates.\n- Start availability and explanations follow planning state, preventing canceled, duplicate and completed inventory from starting new work.\n\n## Diagnose failures without changing the evidence\n\nDoctor runs storage inspection before ordinary startup admission. Missing or incompatible databases can therefore produce diagnostics without initialization or migration, while readable execution evidence, scheduler obligations and installation checks remain available.\n\n- Valid machine-level Execs no longer appear corrupt merely because they have no repository scope. Relative repository paths still fail validation.\n- Missing scheduled receipts remain visible, with the configured executable, log path and reconciliation commands needed to investigate.\n- Binary freshness reports use cached `origin/main`, explicitly identify that limit and show at most three recent commits without fetching.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **Scheduled work:** newly reconciled jobs and CI-watch installations use the stable machine CLI entry point, avoiding binaries retired by installation changes. Existing Sessions retain their runtime ownership. Recovering affected live cron jobs requires installing this release, reconciling the jobs and observing a real scheduled receipt.\n- **Installation:** download, promotion, rollback and recovery no longer depend on Task PR authority. Installation checks remain in place, and installation guidance points to published releases.\n- **Release settlement:** fresh GitHub evidence of a completed merge now lets settlement resume after CI repair instead of stopping on stale failures. The publisher uses `lf release publish` for staging and finalization, fixing the installed-CLI incompatibility that stopped the v0.12.30 publisher.\n- **Skill names:** the former `loopflow` and `review-open-work` skills are consolidated into `repo/operate`; the retired names are removed.\n- **Acceptance limits:** supplied evidence includes focused Rust, Swift and publisher tests. Published upgrade and interrupted-switch recovery, live cron recovery, the complete interactive Task operator workflow, and native Task-history focus and Session-continuation checks remain unverified end to end.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Codex Flow decision schemas now require nullable explanation fields, addressing provider schema rejection while preserving historical receipts.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":0,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":242,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}